n"]}, "visuals": {"outbox": {"items": ["U42"], "count": 1}}}}, {"caption": "2. An eligible worker claims U42. The durable row remains until its outcome is confirmed.", "set": {"nodes": {"worker": ["is-active", "owns U42 attempt"]}}, "packets": [{"edge": "claim", "label": "U42", "tone": "fwd", "kind": "page"}]}, {"caption": "3. Send the operation using the same stable ID U42. Admission into the local outbox was not this server request.", "set": {"nodes": {"server": ["is-active", "processing U42"]}}, "packets": [{"edge": "send", "label": "U42", "tone": "fwd", "kind": "page"}]}, {"caption": "4. The server commits U42, but its reply is lost. The worker cannot infer failure or success from the missing reply; the row remains.", "set": {"nodes": {"worker": ["is-warn", "outcome uncertain"], "server": ["is-done", "U42 committed"], "outbox": ["is-warn", "U42 still pending"]}}}, {"caption": "5. On an eligible retry, send U42 again. The server checks the stable ID instead of performing the mutation twice.", "set": {"nodes": {"worker": ["is-active", "retry U42"], "server": ["is-active", "check stored U42"]}}, "packets": [{"edge": "send", "label": "U42 again", "tone": "fwd", "kind": "page"}]}, {"caption": "6. The server returns its recorded U42 outcome. This example assumes a server contract that retains and deduplicates this ID.", "set": {"nodes": {"worker": ["is-done", "U42 confirmed"], "server": ["is-done", "same committed result"]}}, "packets": [{"edge": "ack", "label": "U42 result", "tone": "back", "kind": "page"}]}, {"caption": "7. Acknowledge U42 in a local transaction and remove its pending row. A crash before this step can cause another safe retry under that server contract.", "set": {"nodes": {"outbox": ["is-done", "no pending U42"], "worker": ["is-done", "acknowledged U42"]}, "visuals": {"outbox": {"items": [], "count": 0}}}, "packets": [{"edge": "remove", "label": "U42 ack", "tone": "back", "kind": "page"}]}]}}}</script>
</section>

Watch the outbox row: claiming it does not delete it, and a missing reply does not justify acknowledgment. A server with no deduplication or result-reconciliation protocol needs a different policy for uncertain non-idempotent work.

<!-- @after Failure Modes :: staff -->
### Bound pending work and processing separately

A capacity-100 Channel bounds its buffer, not every producer coroutine waiting to send. Starting a fresh unowned coroutine per callback can move the backlog outside the buffer. Give processing an owner and make admission failure visible to the caller.

For ordered conversations, serialize work per conversation key. Independent conversations can progress in parallel; global FIFO removal alone does not imply global completion order. Measure oldest-item age and retry/acknowledgment outcomes alongside queue depth.

[Sources: Channel capacity and suspension](https://kotlinlang.org/api/kotlinx.coroutines/kotlinx-coroutines-core/kotlinx.coroutines.channels/-channel/), [per-group FIFO processing](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/using-messagegroupid-property.html).
